## Migrations

SQL files in `migrations/` (`<version>_<name>.up.sql` / `.down.sql`) are embedded into the binary
and applied with golang-migrate when the service starts. Versions run in numeric order and
applied ones are recorded in the `schema_migrations` table.
`projgen add entity` writes its table's migration here, so it runs on the next start.

Test them against a throwaway database:

```bash
TEST_DATABASE_URL=... go test -run 'Migrate|Repository' ./...
```
{{- end}}

## Logging

Logs are JSON with snake_case fields: `@timestamp`, `level`, `message`, `service`, `env`, `request_id`, `logger`.
Keep `message` constant and put dynamic values in their own fields:

```go
logger.FromContext(ctx, log).Info("order created", "order_id", id)
```

Never log passwords, tokens, API keys or personal data.
